	(text "ENCODER DEBOUNCE: RC filter + 74HC14 Schmitt inverter, one stage per contact (A, B, SW).\n10k pulls the contact up to 3V3; R2 10k and C 10n form a 100 us low-pass that\nswallows contact bounce. The slow RC ramp would cross a plain logic threshold several\ntimes; the 74HC14's ~0.9 V hysteresis turns it into a single clean edge, so the Pico\nruns plain edge interrupts with no software debounce. Closed contact reads HIGH at the\nPico (inverted); direction is unaffected since A and B invert together, and the switch\npolarity is handled in config. ENCODER_SW_ACTIVE_HIGH. \n100n decoupling at the 74HC14. Keep the RC parts near the encoder pins;\nthe inverter also isolates the Pico from ESD coupled in through the knob.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 315.468 140.208 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
